{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":2,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1519156218,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE3OlJlbmFtZWRUaXRsZUV2ZW50MTQ4MzIyNjY0Nw=="},"title":"curl call in `annex addurl` does not work with gvfs","was":"curl call in `annex addurl` does not work with gvfs"},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1519156359,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NzA5ODU2NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2208#issuecomment-367098565"},"message":"Thanks for reporting!\n\n@datalad/developers For context: the top-level code that is executed here is a datalad-based shell script that runs in a container (datalad on current master revision). The incompatibility with a gvfs mount is a general datalad/annex issue, though.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1519157206,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NzEwMjYzOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2208#issuecomment-367102638"},"message":"@bpoldrack could it be that this has nothing to do with datalad, but it is simply singularity that did not bind-mount (if it can) the gvfs mount?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1519209107,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NzI4MTQxMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2208#issuecomment-367281412"},"message":"I guess, that's at least a missing pre-condition for this to work, yes!\nGimme a second, I'll try.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1519209739,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NzI4NTE0Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2208#issuecomment-367285142"},"message":"Yes. For me it works with gvfs, if I pass the respective mount point.\n\n@cni-md Please try \n```\nsingularity run --bind /run/user/1002 ../import/cbbs-imaging.simg import /run/user/1002/gvfs/.....\n```\ninstead. Singularity doesn't automatically mount the entire FS for the container. Apart from the user's HOME and CWD, we need to pass needed mount points via `--bind`.\nIt would probably also work to just mount `/run/user` (no permission issue - you are the same user inside as outside), or to be even more specific (like `/run/user/1002/gvfs`)\n\nEdit: Corrected path to container. My local path won't serve you ;-)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"8b17f086a94c7f0c9fd7fb93ddad5ce893006113"},"timestamp":1519222171,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NzMzNzQ0NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2208#issuecomment-367337445"},"message":"With --bind /run/user/1002 it is working now. Thanks a lot","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"8b17f086a94c7f0c9fd7fb93ddad5ce893006113"},"timestamp":1519222171,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTQ4NDczMjkxNA=="},"status":2}]}